From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: sendFrame with a pointer lends the frame instead of copying it

Track::sendFrame(const byte *, size_t, FrameInfo) copied the frame into a message before the media handler
chain, which runs within the call, fragmented it. The frame is now lent (FrameInfo::borrowedData): the
H.264 and H.265 packetizers cut their fragments from the caller's bytes, other packetizers copy as before,
and a track without a handler takes the bytes into the message.
---
--- a/include/rtc/frameinfo.hpp
+++ b/include/rtc/frameinfo.hpp
@@ -25,6 +25,11 @@
